{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Closing an unmerged PR can cause the factory to repeat rejected work without renewed approval, wasting work and resources."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A common alternative dependency format is silently ignored, allowing work to start before its blockers are resolved."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An untrusted collaborator can change an approved issue's title to grant an audit allowance without trusted approval."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A closing reference in quoted issue text can falsely claim another issue and refuse legitimate work on it."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A concurrent start or shutdown during repository resolution can admit an extra queued run, although scheduling still enforces concurrency."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An abnormally distant rate-limit reset overflows the timer and causes repeated rapid wakeups that waste resources."},{"id":"F7","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unverified GitHub-sourced issue run created outside the queue can lose its GitHub status comments when its repository is configured for polling."}]}